;; recovery.aura — restart recovery: re-open the WAL and replay frames
;; This is the high-level recovery driver: takes a (possibly torn) WAL,
;; invokes the repair pass, then re-opens by rebuilding the log from
;; the surviving sectors and counting what was recovered.

;; Recover a WAL by:
;;   1. Running the scan-and-repair pass to fix any torn sectors.
;;   2. Replaying frames from the (now-consistent) sector stream.
;;   3. Returning the list of replayed frames.
;;
;; The repair pass itself truncates the partial sector or rebuilds it from
;; prior committed frames; after that, the WAL is consistent and replay
;; yields a deterministic frame list.
(define (api recovery-run w)
  (begin
    (repair-scan w)
    (replay-frames w)))
